===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|music}} To sing in the fifth voice in a polyphonic melody.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1996|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=2MhogmU1lpUC&pg=PA510|title=Music in Early English Religious Drama: Minstrels playing|page=510
|passage=Another extension of strict organum is 'fifthing'. '''Fifthing''' is a note-against- note method of creating a two-part texture by improvising a second voice over the given tune, starting and ending each musical phrase at the octave and proceeding mainly in fifths above the tune at others times.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1978|url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/932295|title=Discant and the Theory of Fifthing
|passage=Each of these three groups contributes some special insight into the nature of fifthing and the context in which it was practiced.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To support something fifth, after four others have already done so.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2017|url=http://www.indiewire.com/2017/11/tv-shows-mental-health-homeland-hannibal-1201897306/|title=Critics Pick the TV Shows That Get Mental Health Right — IndieWire Survey
|passage=Though seconding (or '''fifthing''') the praise for “BoJack Horseman” and “In Treatment,” I think I’ll use the majority of my space to discuss “You’re the Worst.”}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|nonstandard}} To divide by five.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=0kOJvLyf55wC&pg=PA188|title=Mathematics for Dyslexics: Including Dyscalculia|page=188
|passage=3/5 has been through '''fifthing'''. 2/3 has been through thirding. Therefore, 3/5 now needs thirding and 2/3 needs '''fifthing'''}}

